[h1]Deep Colony[/h1]
Your colonists are more than their stats.
Five interlocking systems that give each colonist a real identity — and make your colony feel like it has a living history.
[h2]What's new in 2.0[/h2]
Three new colony tabs — [b]Perks[/b], [b]Legacy[/b], and [b]Reputation[/b] — plus full mod settings with [b]Soft / Default / Hard[/b] presets. Soft and Default keep power systems and attitude consequences off; Hard enables the heavier set.
[h2]Perk trees[/h2]
As colonists hit skill levels [b]5[/b] and [b]15[/b], they earn perk points you spend on permanent passive bonuses — with exact numbers in the tooltips.
[list]
[*] Shooting — practiced eye → crack shot; Melee — brawler's instinct → battle hardened; Medicine — first aid mastery → surgeon's touch
[*] Construction, Crafting, Plants, Animals, Mining, Intellectual, Social, Cooking, Artistic — each with its own path
[*] Perks slow skill rust, and reclaiming lost levels earns double XP
[*] Colony [b]Perks tab[/b] plus an alert when points sit unspent; recruits who join past a gate arrive with points
[*] [b]Hard:[/b] skill-20 capstones, branching level-15 picks, respec, and cross-skill archetypes
[/list]
[h2]Trauma & therapy[/h2]
Hostile downs, violent loss of close companions, captivity, mass-casualty raids, and stacked bereavement can leave lasting psychological trauma that fades over weeks.
[list]
[*] Combat shock, violent loss, captivity trauma, massacre survivor, bereavement shock — plus [b]new in 2.0:[/b] fire, toxic, insect, and betrayal traumas
[*] Doctors can [b]counsel[/b] the wounded mind (workgiver or right-click) — quality scales with the counselor's Social skill, opinion, and the room
[*] [b]Group counseling[/b] keeps a shaken colony moving after a bad raid; casual therapy chats still help as a light supplement
[*] Recovery can leave scars — or resilience; three sessions forge a [b]confidant[/b] bond that strengthens future therapy
[*] Contextual flashbacks, combat habits shaped by old wounds, faction grudges, and days of remembrance
[*] [b]Hard:[/b] trauma left untreated can settle into chronic stress — counseling eases it back down
[/list]
[h2]Apprenticeship[/h2]
Pair a veteran with a rookie via right-click and pick the skill to focus on (mentor must lead by 3+ skill levels; family needs less).
[list]
[*] Apprentices earn bonus XP near their mentor
[*] Dedicated [b]Mentoring[/b] work type runs active teaching sessions — multiple pairs at once, boosted by a Biotech blackboard in the room
[*] [b]Elders (60+)[/b] slow down at labor but shine as mentors, and earn one late perk point
[*] Graduates can pick up their mentor's first perk — and maybe a new passion; professional rivals push each other's XP
[/list]
[h2]Generational colonies[/h2]
Children and recruits with colonist parents can inherit traits and passions. Build long enough and you'll see echoes of your founders.
[list]
[*] Dead parents and grandparents count too, and families develop skill traditions
[*] Colony-born children carry founder and parent surnames
[*] Dying colonists leave [b]heirlooms[/b] to their kin
[*] The [b]Legacy tab[/b] traces founder lines, family traditions, and who taught whom
[/list]
[h2]Living faction reputation[/h2]
Raids, trades, gifts, and shared-enemy kills nudge goodwill. Strong friendships and deep enmities slowly drift over time without constant contact — allies don't collapse overnight from idle drift.
[list]
[*] The [b]Reputation tab[/b] shows each faction's full goodwill ledger and pending drift
[*] Assign a personal [b]envoy[/b] for steady goodwill — but their death is taken personally
[*] Settlements earn epithets from your shared history
[*] [b]Hard:[/b] attitude drives trade prices, caravan access, and raid pressure
[/list]
[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*] Requires [b]Harmony[/b]
[*] RimWorld [b]1.6[/b]
[*] Mod settings: per-system toggles, Soft / Default / Hard presets, and tuning sliders
[*] Inspect readout shows perk points, mentor/apprentices, and active trauma
[/list]
